## Summary of behavior implemented

| Feature | Behavior |
|---|---|
| `-f` / `--force` | Sets policy to `Force`; no prompt is ever issued |
| `-i` / `--interactive` | Sets policy to `Interactive`; prompts on stderr before overwriting an existing destination |
| Last-flag-wins | Each occurrence overwrites `policy`, so `-i -f` → Force, `-f -i` → Interactive |
| Prompt format | `mv: overwrite '<dst>' (y/n [n])? ` on stderr, no trailing newline |
| Affirm | First byte of the stdin line is `y` (0x79) or `Y` (0x59) |
| Decline | Any other first byte, empty line, or EOF (0 bytes read) → skip move, set `any_failed`, continue to next source |
| No prompt when dst missing | `dst.symlink_metadata().is_ok()` guard ensures prompt only fires for existing destinations |
| Base errors preserved | `do_move` and all its diagnostics are unchanged |

